class Solution {
    public boolean canJump(int[] nums) {
        int maxReachable = 0;
        
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            // If the current index is beyond our reach, we can't progress
            if (i > maxReachable) {
                return false;
            }
            
            // Update the maximum index we can reach
            maxReachable = Math.max(maxReachable, i + nums[i]);
            
            // Early exit: if we can already reach or pass the final index
            if (maxReachable >= nums.length - 1) {
                return true;
            }
        }
        
        return true;
    }
}
CODE END
 Single linear scanSpace Complexity O(n) 
 Only one variable (maxReachable) O(1) 
